- Story & Context: Stranded at the switchyard of Carbondale Junction with a blown wagon tire while the midday sky rapidly bruised to violet, keyboardist Madam Pendula pounded her celesta’s keys until her knuckles bled magenta carnival chalk. The local freight-train conductor tried to issue her a trespassing warning, but the sheer velocity of the slapback upright bass made his clipboard rattle straight out of his trembling hands. Over a squelching electro-pop bassline and frantic, clapping snare rolls, Pendula shrieked her joyful confession to the gathered hobos: "I lost the calendar but found the beat that stops the world!"
