- Story & Context: Legend says that after the carnival vanished from Snake Valley following totality, every municipal clock tower across three counties began chiming in syncopated slapback triplets instead of on the hour. County sheriffs discovered only a scorched ring of glitter, several shattered vacuum tubes, and a melted celesta hammer left behind on the desert floor. A high-school radio station receiver picked up the lingering broadcast loop fading into the ionosphere, a joyous gang-vocal hook that refused to wind down: "Don't wind that cog back up, honey, we're living in the slip!"
